      "anchorText": "Hanc deus et melior litem natura diremit.",
      "body": "Line 24. Both Deus (\"quisquis deum...\" whoever of the gods it was...) and melior natura (nature meaning natural processes; melior meaning better than the chaos that came before) are what assembled the world. Thus the Stoics who demanded a Demiurge were satisfied, and the Epicureans too, who said it was Nature. Ovid had it both ways.",
      "createdAt": 1781298961103,
      "updatedAt": 1781443029790,
      "resolvedAt": null
    },
